        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a faithful, additive copy of the codebase's established validation idiom:\n\n- `RegistrationDateValidator` mirrors `PostcodeValidator` precisely \u2014 `final` class, private constructor, a single static `validate(...)`, the same null-skips-validation convention, and the same Javadoc style. A maintainer would find it entirely natural.\n- `InvalidRegistrationDateException` mirrors `InvalidPostcodeException` (a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending values into its message), living alongside it in `util`.\n- The new `handleInvalidRegistrationDateException` handler slots into `ExceptionControllerAdvice` next to the existing handlers, reusing `detailBuild`, `ERROR_INVALID_REQUEST`, and the same logging/status pattern \u2014 the right unit for mapping domain exceptions to HTTP responses.\n- Placement of the validator call in `addOwner` is correct and complete: `OwnerRestControllerV2` has no owner-creation endpoint, and `updateOwner` never sets `registrationDate`, so there is no missing call site and no duplication.\n\nLogic is in the right place, nothing is duplicated, and no class is turning into a catch-all."
